 "remarks": "The opportunity to create a residence of lasting architectural significance begins with an extraordinary setting.  On New Canaan's coveted West Side, conceptual plans envision a custom residence of approximately 6,000 to 8,000+ square feet, thoughtfully positioned within an offering of 4.91 acres bordering 42 acres of permanently protected land trust.  Comprising two approved building lots at 230 West Road (2.34 acres) and 244 West Road (2.57 acres), the property offers the flexibility to consider a substantial private estate or two individually designed residences. The surrounding landscape, established estate properties, and proximity to New Canaan's village provide a compelling foundation for an ambitious architectural undertaking.  The proposed renderings offer a glimpse of what might be achieved, while leaving the ultimate expression of the home to its future owner. From architectural style and spatial composition to the relationship between indoor and outdoor living, every element presents an opportunity for a distinctly personal interpretation.  Residence shown is conceptual and has not been constructed. List price is for land only; construction costs are additional. Proposed design is subject to applicable approvals.",
